{"title":"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> be an integer and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18eecdd2d8a05a3cc1435bc57ff52fcbee7b6e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell \\in\\{1,2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />. A collection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd59ab493cf4f21d3f8e1c44db1ff4625eca9d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, \\ldots, A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> of (not necessarily distinct) subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc169aff5a3045cd7bca6cf7050eb325ec1fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> is called <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />-large if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1fc566dbfcd599afd1f71394f3a32318ca4fa34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|A_i\\right| \\geq \\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28c82ec9d7adbeb949d4233e8eadafd3b7d2ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i \\leq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. Find, in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />, the largest real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed5047ee81526de349e5b0029f19c0187c25429.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^k \\sum_{j=1}^k x_i x_j \\frac{\\left|A_i \\cap A_j\\right|^2}{\\left|A_i\\right| \\cdot\\left|A_j\\right|} \\geq c\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^k x_i\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"59\" />\nholds for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, all nonnegative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124f55009149f42b54d9df5dadddb187f5d7b420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\ldots, x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />-large collections <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd59ab493cf4f21d3f8e1c44db1ff4625eca9d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, \\ldots, A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> of subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc169aff5a3045cd7bca6cf7050eb325ec1fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note: For a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/703d476da77d88fa4cb8a6b30ca4dfcc1a8da95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,|S|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26095afa05153cfe0a0ffafd016348b3659b240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n - 2\\ell + \\ell^2}{n(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"93\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28c82ec9d7adbeb949d4233e8eadafd3b7d2ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i \\leq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4b62206d02b839e0959772e8cd42e685f86ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{1}_{A_i} : \\{1, 2, \\ldots, n\\} \\to \\{0, 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" /> denote the indicator function of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. We can rewrite the intersection size in the numerator as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83ddfc05ce5c7933f7aaf4bffcd4e62df19e0ce3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|A_i \\cap A_j|^2 = \\left( \\sum_{m=1}^n \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m) \\mathbf{1}_{A_j}(m) \\right)^2 = \\sum_{m=1}^n \\sum_{m&#39;=1}^n \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m) \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m&#39;) \\mathbf{1}_{A_j}(m) \\mathbf{1}_{A_j}(m&#39;).\\]\" width=\"606\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Substitute this into the original double sum and rearrange the order of summation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961f3258bd3a5ca6833f529b273e152c48a92186.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^k \\sum_{j=1}^k x_i x_j \\frac{|A_i \\cap A_j|^2}{|A_i| \\cdot |A_j|} = \\sum_{m=1}^n \\sum_{m&#39;=1}^n \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^k \\frac{x_i}{|A_i|} \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m) \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m&#39;) \\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"486\" height=\"59\" />\n</p><p>Define a symmetric <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> where the entry in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />-th row and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644b1d79ecab35999ad2f46649f0676cd91d1af5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />-th column is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81911d92d2abd43ea0a3037b764917a6ad5a7f40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[W_{m, m&#39;} = \\sum_{i=1}^k \\frac{x_i}{|A_i|} \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m) \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m&#39;).\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>The expression we wish to bound is the sum of the squares of all entries in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, which we can split into diagonal and off-diagonal sums:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7886e9a066a637341d185e7b1fdb65db107a9345.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m, m&#39;} W_{m, m&#39;}^2 = \\sum_{m=1}^n W_{m,m}^2 + \\sum_{m \\neq m&#39;} W_{m, m&#39;}^2.\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, the sum of squares of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> elements is bounded below by the square of their sum divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Applying this to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> diagonal elements and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d3407c16ac230a65d2dbb640f0d46dfe4e1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> off-diagonal elements separately yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be66bcdb0b18922e22ba8195b72dac059f5d457f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m=1}^n W_{m,m}^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{n} \\left( \\sum_{m=1}^n W_{m,m} \\right)^2\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"57\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fae8209ca5952c07685df537ee066d59f7dc85e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m \\neq m&#39;} W_{m,m&#39;}^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{n(n-1)} \\left( \\sum_{m \\neq m&#39;} W_{m,m&#39;} \\right)^2\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Next, we evaluate the sums of these entries. The sum of the diagonal elements (the trace) is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21c631a6c59fc7d8a81109edda7fdec134e2f0a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m=1}^n W_{m,m} = \\sum_{i=1}^k \\frac{x_i}{|A_i|} \\sum_{m=1}^n \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m) = \\sum_{i=1}^k \\frac{x_i}{|A_i|} |A_i| = \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i.\\]\" width=\"442\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>The sum of all entries in the matrix is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d4221797f2916f861d6e372a2ff5cc1b433da600.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m, m&#39;} W_{m, m&#39;} = \\sum_{i=1}^k \\frac{x_i}{|A_i|} \\left( \\sum_{m=1}^n \\mathbf{1}_{A_i}(m) \\right)^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i |A_i|.\\]\" width=\"399\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the trace from the total sum gives the sum of the off-diagonal elements:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b75b7b7b50c313baa4069eb16d9ca1cec3afed0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m \\neq m&#39;} W_{m, m&#39;} = \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i |A_i| - \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i = \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i (|A_i| - 1).\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Because the collection is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />-large, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/5684cc73dfbc70ec56ee78ec3190687845ea5880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_i| \\geq \\ell \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />. Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7db9278c5bd9ab527b14e789304bfc769df7af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc9e0397baa12d95952bdcf78b352df1fe04969c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m \\neq m&#39;} W_{m, m&#39;} \\geq \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i (\\ell - 1) = (\\ell - 1) \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i \\geq 0.\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0765820e58c39918effd560ebaeac48a5ade73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\sum_{i=1}^k x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"83\" height=\"56\" />. Substituting these into our Cauchy-Schwarz bounds:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98b8879a3301905dba325716e41d3f5c8ce9594.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m, m&#39;} W_{m, m&#39;}^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{n} S^2 + \\frac{1}{n(n-1)} (\\ell - 1)^2 S^2 = \\left( \\frac{n - 1 + (\\ell - 1)^2}{n(n-1)} \\right) S^2 = \\frac{n - 2\\ell + \\ell^2}{n(n-1)} S^2.\\]\" width=\"641\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>This establishes that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b3119ea43a9582601cc9a3d4c5a5700112f34c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{n - 2\\ell + \\ell^2}{n(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"125\" height=\"45\" /> is a valid lower bound. \n</p><p>To show this bound is achievable, consider the collection of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d004e37328a60a322c33fa5d50673bb196defddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\binom{n}{\\ell}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"75\" height=\"55\" /> distinct subsets of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c75eb8978ee0840709244e93e95693ba1825888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. By symmetry, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> diagonal entries of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> are identical, and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d3407c16ac230a65d2dbb640f0d46dfe4e1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> off-diagonal entries are identical. Thus, the equality condition holds for both applications of Cauchy-Schwarz, confirming the maximum constant is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26095afa05153cfe0a0ffafd016348b3659b240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n - 2\\ell + \\ell^2}{n(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"93\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO\" title=\"2024 USAMO\">2024 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017043959\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 323/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1282/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11355/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.364      1 -total\n 59.31%    7.333      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 39.02%    4.824      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27282:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017043959 and revision id 291164. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}